PASSWORD MANAGER - SECURE PASSWORD STORAGE
================================================================================

A desktop password management application built with Python and Tkinter. The app
generates strong passwords, stores them securely in a JSON file, and allows
quick retrieval of saved credentials.

================================================================================
PROJECT OVERVIEW
================================================================================

Password Manager is a secure application that:

Generates strong, random passwords with letters, numbers, and symbols

Saves website credentials (email/username and password) to a JSON file

Searches for and displays saved passwords for specific websites

Copies generated passwords to clipboard automatically

Validates input fields before saving

================================================================================
HOW TO USE
================================================================================

Add a New Password:

Enter the website name

Enter your email/username

Click "Generate Password" or type your own password

Click "Add" to save

Generate a Password:

Click "Generate Password" button

A strong password (12-18 characters) is created

Password is automatically copied to clipboard

Search for Credentials:

Enter a website name

Click "Search" button

If found, email and password are displayed in a popup

================================================================================
PASSWORD GENERATION
================================================================================

Generated passwords include:

8-10 random letters (uppercase and lowercase)

2-4 random numbers

2-4 random symbols (! # $ % & ( ) * +)

Shuffled for randomness

12-18 characters total length

================================================================================
PROJECT STRUCTURE
================================================================================

password-manager/
├── main.py # Main application file
├── data.json # Password storage (created automatically)
├── logo.png # Application logo
├── requirements.txt # Python dependencies
└── README.txt # This file

================================================================================
INSTALLATION & SETUP
================================================================================

Install required packages:
pip install -r requirements.txt

Or manually:
pip install pyperclip

Ensure logo.png is in the project folder

Run the application:
python main.py

================================================================================
DATA STORAGE FORMAT
================================================================================

Passwords are stored in data.json with this format:

{
"website.com": {
"email": "user@email.com",
"password": "GeneratedPassword123!"
},
"another-site.com": {
"email": "user@email.com",
"password": "AnotherPass456#"
}
}

================================================================================
SECURITY NOTES
================================================================================

⚠️ IMPORTANT SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS:

This app stores passwords in PLAIN TEXT in a JSON file

NOT recommended for production use without encryption

For learning purposes only

Consider adding encryption for real-world use

Keep the data.json file secure and backed up

================================================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

ISSUE: 'pyperclip' module not found
SOLUTION: pip install pyperclip

ISSUE: Logo not displaying
SOLUTION: Ensure logo.png is in the project folder

ISSUE: Search returns "No Data File Found"
SOLUTION: Add at least one password first to create data.json

ISSUE: Empty fields error
SOLUTION: Fill in all required fields before saving

================================================================================
TIPS FOR USE
================================================================================

Use the "Generate Password" button for strong, random passwords

The generated password is automatically copied to your clipboard

Use "Search" to quickly retrieve passwords without scrolling

Keep your data.json file backed up

Default email can be changed in the code

